ERA I  RELATIVITY WORKSHOP  c.1912-1955
================================================================

EINSTEIN

TYPE
  handwritten research notebooks (used both ends)
  loose working sheets
  letters as proto-papers
  blackboard
  later: scratch sheets for unified field attempts

CORE OBJECTS / VARIABLES
  x^mu              coordinates  mu = 0,1,2,3
  dx^mu             coordinate differentials
  ds^2              line element
  g_mu nu           metric  (early pages: G_mu nu, then g)
  g^mu nu           inverse metric
  g                 det(g_mu nu), often as sqrt(-g)
  T_mu nu           stress-energy
  Gamma^lambda_mu nu   Christoffel symbols
  R^rho_sigma mu nu    Riemann  (early: four-index symbol (i kappa, lm))
  R_mu nu           Ricci
  R                 Ricci scalar
  G_mu nu           Einstein tensor (later standard)
  T_il              notebook stand-in for Ricci-like candidates

FUNDAMENTALS
  tensor = array of components labeled by indices
  repeated index => sum          (Einstein summation, 1916)
  raise / lower with g_mu nu or g^mu nu
  contraction = set two indices equal and sum
  covariance tested by transformation law, not by a picture
  derivative path:  partial_mu  then  nabla_mu

HOW OPERATIONS LOOK ON THE PAGE
  power / root     superscripts,  sqrt(-g)
  derivative       d/dx^mu  written out; later nabla
  product          juxtaposition of tensors
  equality         next line rewritten
  failed ansatz    left on the page, not erased

QUIRKS
  notation drift inside a few pages (G -> g)
  margin tags: Grossmann tensor fourth rank / Stimmt
  neat two-page fair copy only after the result is believed
  double strategy visible: covariant candidate, Newtonian test, discard


ERA II  DIAGRAMMATIC QFT  c.1940s-1960s
================================================================

FEYNMAN

TYPE
  student notebooks with ToC and copied figures
  lecture boards
  paper margins
  published papers where the graph IS the term

CORE OBJECTS / VARIABLES
  line              propagator
  vertex            interaction
  loop              integral over internal momentum
  p, k, q           four-momenta
  m                 mass in denominator p^2 - m^2
  e, g, lambda      couplings  (power = vertex count)
  gamma^mu          Dirac matrices
  A-slash           A/ = gamma^mu A_mu
  S[x]              action
  Dx                path-integral measure
  G(x2,t2; x1,t1)   Green function / fermion line

LINE TYPES (community later standardized)
  solid             fermion
  wavy              vector boson / photon
  dashed            scalar
  arrow             charge / fermion flow

FUNDAMENTALS
  a diagram is a well-formed expression, not an illustration
  join lines        multiply amplitudes
  close a loop      integrate d^4k / (2pi)^4
  reverse an arrow  conjugate / antiparticle
  count vertices    order in perturbation theory
  early reading     spacetime worldlines
  later reading     momentum-space graphs

HOW OPERATIONS LOOK ON THE PAGE
  product           vertex
  contraction       index routed along a line, or closed loop
  derivative        extra insertion / extra line
  integral          loop, or product of ordinary integrals -> path integral
  equality          two graphs with the same external legs

QUIRKS
  doodles next to operator chains
  informal shorthand for repeated integrals
  slash notation as compressed Dirac algebra
  visual left-to-right "do this then that"


ERA III  VISUAL TENSOR LOGIC  c.1960s-1980s
================================================================

PENROSE

TYPE  (three separate picture systems)
  1 graphical tensor notation / tensor diagrams   1971
  2 twistor diagrams
  3 Penrose-Carter conformal spacetime diagrams
  plus: abstract index notation as the symbolic twin
  plus: spin networks

CORE OBJECTS / VARIABLES
  blob + wires      tensor
  open wire         free index
  joined wires      contracted indices
  loop              trace
  T_a b^c           abstract indices  (basis-free)
  A, A'             unprimed / primed spinor indices
  Z^alpha           twistor        (black vertex)
  W_alpha           dual twistor   (white vertex)
  W.Z               incidence / propagator power
  homogeneity n     twistor function weight

SPACETIME-DIAGRAM VARIABLES (system 3, different job)
  i^0               spatial infinity
  i+, i-            future / past timelike infinity
  I+, I-            future / past null infinity
  45-degree rays    null geodesics

FUNDAMENTALS
  index routing should be visible at a glance
  contraction is plumbing, not dummy-index bookkeeping
  planar isotopy of wires = same expression
  dualize by redirecting or recoloring
  twistor edge ~ (W_alpha Z^alpha)^n encodes a contour integral
  conformal diagram compactifies infinity; it is causal geometry,
  not tensor algebra

HOW OPERATIONS LOOK ON THE PAGE
  product / compose     stack or plumb diagrams
  contract / trace      connect two wires / close a loop
  sym / antisym         bars or hooks on a wire bundle
  covariant derivative  mark on a line
  dualize               black <-> white, or raise/lower wire
  equality              rewrite rule or diagram deformation

QUIRKS
  drawn for private calculation; hard to typeset
  revolt against multi-index soup
  same visual habit feeds tilings, impossible figures, spin nets


ERA IV  HYBRID PRESENT  c.1990s-now
================================================================

CONTEMPORARY THEORISTS

TYPE
  paper or tablet first contact
  CAS notebooks     Mathematica Sage Maple Cadabra xAct
  LaTeX + TikZ / tikzit / feynmp / JaxoDraw
  Jupyter / plain git-tracked files
  public artifact still looks like a 1970s paper with better figures

CORE OBJECTS / VARIABLES  (several dialects at once)
  g_mu nu, R_mu nu, T_mu nu     Einstein indices still default in GR/QFT
  T_ab^c                        abstract indices when basis-free
  |psi>, <phi|, O               Dirac on Hilbert space
  Feynman lines + p,k,m         perturbative QFT
  wires / cups / caps           string diagrams, ZX, birdtracks
  objects, morphisms, 2-cells   category / TQFT
  I_family, symbol letters      modern Feynman-integral technology

TOOL VARIABLES
  nabla, partial, delta/delta phi
  Contract, Simplify, Collect   CAS verbs
  commit / diff                 version of a derivation

FUNDAMENTALS
  no single winner
  think in pictures or indices
  verify in computer algebra
  publish in Einstein-dialect LaTeX
  diagrams from code, not only from the hand
  category diagrams treat composition as the primitive

HOW OPERATIONS LOOK ON THE PAGE / SCREEN
  power / root / deriv     LaTeX macros or CAS operators
  product                  juxtaposition, vertex, or string compose
  contract                 dummy index or wire or Contract[]
  integral                 loop + master-integral / symbol alphabet
  equality                 lemma environment + git history

QUIRKS
  private handwriting still Einstein + Feynman
  two cultures: index-heavy GR/QFT vs diagram-heavy categorical work
  iterative rewriting hidden inside the CAS until export


SAME OPERATIONS, FOUR HANDS
================================================================

MULTIPLY / COMPOSE
  Einstein        juxtapose tensors, sum repeated indices
  Feynman         join lines at a vertex
  Penrose         stack or plumb diagrams
  now             CAS product, or string-diagram compose

CONTRACT / TRACE
  Einstein        repeat an index
  Feynman         close a loop
  Penrose         connect two wires
  now             dummy index  or  wire  or  Contract command

DIFFERENTIATE
  Einstein        partial_mu then nabla_mu
  Feynman         vertex insertion / extra line
  Penrose         mark on a wire
  now             nabla, functional delta/delta phi

INTEGRATE
  Einstein        int d^4x sqrt(-g)
  Feynman         loop  int d^4k/(2pi)^4  or  path integral Dx
  Penrose         contour in twistor space
  now             Feynman integral families + symbols

DUALIZE / RAISE-LOWER
  Einstein        explicit g_mu nu
  Feynman         slash, charge conjugate, reverse arrow
  Penrose         black <-> white, redirect wire
  now             metric macros, dagger

EQUALITY
  Einstein        rewrite the next line
  Feynman         two graphs, same external legs
  Penrose         planar isotopy / rewrite rule
  now             lemma + commit


INHERITANCE
================================================================

Ricci-Levi-Civita index calculus
  -> Einstein page language
  -> still the default journal dialect

Feynman graphs-as-terms
  -> perturbative QFT
  -> permission for a drawing to BE the calculation

Penrose wires-as-indices
  -> tensor networks, string diagrams, ZX, birdtracks

present toolchain
  hosts all three
  adds CAS + version control
  does not replace them


